  "_comment": "Clan prize pools (e.g. Dark Omens) that the game hands the whole clan as a single lump of dragon coins (a kind-9 event), which the leader then shares out by participation points. Each payout looks exactly like a normal tournament repayment in the captures (a kind-1 dragon-coin event), so build_state.py pulls the per-member shares recorded here out of 'received' and keeps them in a separate pool flow — otherwise they cancel tournament coins that were never actually repaid and hide who is still owed. 'coins' is what each member was paid from the pool; 'total' is what the clan received. 'paidOut' marks a pool whose shares have actually been handed out as kind-1 payouts (so they are carved out of 'received' to keep the tournament reconciliation honest); a pool still sitting in clan storage is paidOut:false and left untouched until it is distributed.",
